## [P2] Dispose launched process handles during cleanup

`Start-TargetProcess` retains each `Process` in `$script:launched`, but `Stop-LaunchedProcesses` never disposes those objects. Higher iteration counts can accumulate open handles until the script exits. Add the cleanup in `finally` so the handle is released even when stopping fails or the process has already exited.

```suggestion
        }
        finally
        {
            $process.Dispose()
        }
```

### [P2] (1/2) Average the middle samples for an even count

**Severity:** `medium`

The default run collects 10 measured samples, but nearest-rank p50 returns only the lower middle value. That is not the conventional median for an even-sized sample and can bias the reported benchmark result downward. Average the two middle values for p50 while retaining nearest-rank behavior for p90; apply together with (2/2).

```suggestion
    if ($Percentile -eq 0.5 -and $sorted.Count % 2 -eq 0)
    {
        $middle = [int]($sorted.Count / 2)
        return [Math]::Round(($sorted[$middle - 1] + $sorted[$middle]) / 2, 1)
    }
    $index = [Math]::Max(0, [Math]::Ceiling($Percentile * $sorted.Count) - 1)
```
